00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:48.387
empty and therefore he
flagged the execution as a

00:05:48.387 --> 00:05:53.887
success. And again, the common
problem here is most of

00:05:53.887 --> 00:05:59.140
the hardest problems to detect are not
the ones that explicitly say there was an

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.660
error, are the ones that
say success, right?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.213
So, it has a success tag and you assume
everything is okay, but a lot of

00:06:07.213 --> 00:06:12.013
times the success hides
deeper problems that

00:06:12.013 --> 00:06:17.300
via having your own n8n server,

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:21.000
you can actually, this is a fact that as
