00:06:30.047 --> 00:06:34.847
to solve each, but I'm
going to skip that in order

00:06:34.847 --> 00:06:39.920
to speed up. I also had a problem with
an if node, that was a formula that

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.000
was only compatible with an older
version of n8n, and therefore it

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:49.820
assumed this formula was also
compatible with the current n8n version

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:54.880
with which I was running, and therefore
it would simply choose the wrong gates

00:06:54.880 --> 00:07:00.040
and assume the rules were false
and proceed to the next step on

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.460
a classification that was simply wrong.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.853
And of course, the execution
in the end ran as normal and

00:07:07.853 --> 00:07:10.613
the step was classified as successful.

00:07:10.847 --> 00:07:13.207
Now I have also another example.

